! The gerund leaders of `ahead.dict`: the word before the hole, stroked first,
! and the hole takes an -ing.
!
! Its own directory, and not part of `tests/frames`, because what these prove is
! the inflection: `{:infl:ing}` is a lexicon, so it needs the artifacts in
! `build/morph`, and whether those are built is a property of the machine.
! `check.sh` skips this the way it skips the other morphology checks.
!
! Nothing here reads the word. The tail waits for the unit after it, and the
! host joins it: `scripts/check-hold.py` asks Plover the same questions.

! ---- the ordinary case, including what a rule would get wrong
!buffer
^PW*EU
RUPB
!buffer
^A*F
HRAOEUBG
!buffer
^KAO*EP
STOP
!buffer
^WHAO*EUL
KAER
!buffer
^STO*P
TKPW

! ---- a unit that writes nothing does not take the tail
!buffer
^PW*EU
KHR-BG
RUPB

! ---- a second leader before the first has landed
! The tail waits for text, and the second leader's own word is text, so the
! first tail lands on that: "by keeping", and then the second tail waits for the
! word. Both hosts do it, and a writer who wanted "by keep running" has
! mis-stroked rather than found a corner.
!buffer
^PW*EU
^KAO*EP
RUPB

! ---- undo puts the tail back, because the mark carries it
!buffer
^STO*P
RUPB
!undo
TKPW

! ---- what a tail shows while it waits
! A suffix has no word to join yet, so it shows as a suffix reads: "by -ing",
! and the hyphen is where the word goes.
!buffer
^PW*EU
!buffer
^PW*EU
KHR-BG
